#. Confirmation text; {task} is the title of a checklist task, such as
#. "Open Talk"
msgid "\"{task}\" goes from everyone's list."
msgstr ""

#. {from} and {until} are dates, such as "Oct 9, 2026"; the period in which
#. a tour starts by itself
msgid "{from} to {until}"
msgstr ""

#. {tour} is the name of a tour, such as "Talk"
msgid "{tour} will be shown again"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the tour of the IntroVox administration page. Words in
#. bold are names of tabs and buttons on that page: use the same
#. translation
msgid "<ol><li><strong>Add step</strong>, and give it a title and a text.</li><li><strong>Pick element</strong>: click what the step should point at, anywhere in Nextcloud.</li><li><strong>Test this step</strong> to see it as others will.</li><li><strong>Save</strong>. It is live straight away.</li></ol>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Calendar app. Words in bold
#. are labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p><strong>Calendar settings</strong> has the CalDAV address for your phone or Thunderbird, and a separate one for iPhone and Mac. On Android, use the DAVx⁵ app.</p><p>Sign in there with an app password, made in your personal settings under <strong>Security</strong>.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the welcome tour. Words in bold are names in
#. Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p><strong>Did you know:</strong></p><ul><li>You can upload files by dragging them to your browser</li><li>You can directly share files with a link</li><li>You can also use Nextcloud as an app on your phone</li><li>All your data is stored privately and securely</li></ul>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the welcome tour. Words in bold are names in
#. Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p><strong>Finding your way around:</strong></p><ul><li>Use the <strong>apps menu</strong> (top left) to switch between apps</li><li>Open your <strong>avatar</strong> (top right) for your account and settings</li><li>Use the <strong>search bar</strong> to quickly find files and more</li></ul>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Talk app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p><strong>Home</strong> shows your upcoming meetings, unread mentions and message reminders.</p><p>Search your phone's app store for Nextcloud Talk, so calls and messages reach you when this tab is closed.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the welcome tour. Words in bold are names in
#. Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p><strong>Nextcloud is your personal cloud storage!</strong></p><p>Here you can:</p><ul><li>📁 Upload, share and collaborate on files</li><li>📅 Manage your calendar</li><li>✉️ Send and receive email</li><li>👥 Keep track of contacts</li></ul>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the tour of the IntroVox administration page. Words in
#. bold are names of tabs and buttons on that page: use the same
#. translation
msgid "<p><strong>Preview tour</strong> runs the whole tour as people get it, as a member of a group if you like. A preview is not counted in the statistics.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the tour of the IntroVox administration page. Words in
#. bold are names of tabs and buttons on that page: use the same
#. translation
msgid "<p><strong>Settings</strong> switches tours on for everyone, <strong>Tours</strong> is where you write them, <strong>Statistics</strong> shows how many people start and finish the welcome tour, and <strong>Support</strong> is where to find help.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Talk app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>A group conversation keeps a team's messages, files and calls in one place, instead of long email threads.</p><p>Let's make one: click the highlighted button. If it is not there, click <strong>Home</strong> at the top left.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Calendar app. Words in bold
#. are labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Add colleagues, or anyone by email, under <strong>Attendees</strong>. Once they are added, <strong>Find a time</strong> in <strong>More details</strong> shows when they are free. Reminders are there too.</p><p>To invite people, your account needs an email address. First, the basics.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Files app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Changed a file by mistake? In its details, <strong>Versions</strong> brings back an earlier one. Deleted something? It stays in <strong>Deleted files</strong> for a while.</p><p>That's it. Now drag your files into your folder, and send links instead of attachments.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Talk app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Chat, calls and video meetings with your colleagues, right next to your files.</p><p>In this tour you set up a conversation for your team, add colleagues and see how calls, meetings and notifications work.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Calendar app. Words in bold
#. are labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Click <strong>Save</strong>, and your event is in your calendar. Later, click it to see or edit it, or drag it to another day or time.</p><p>Rather not keep it? Close it with ✕, then click <strong>Next</strong>.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Calendar app. Words in bold
#. are labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Click a calendar to show or hide its events. You may also see birthdays, Deck cards with a due date and calendars shared with you.</p><p>To share one, hover over it and choose <strong>Edit and share calendar</strong>.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Deck app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Click in the field, type a real task, such as <em>Set up a board for my project</em>, and press <strong>Enter</strong>. Your card appears in the list and the field empties.</p><p>Only Enter saves it, so press Enter first, then click <strong>Next</strong>.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Deck app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Click the <strong>+</strong> here and pick a date. Cards with a due date come back in <strong>Upcoming cards</strong> and, if you use Calendar, in your calendar.</p><p>On a shared board, you can assign the card to someone in the field above; they get a notification.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Talk app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Click the highlighted button to create the conversation.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Files app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Copy the <strong>Internal link</strong> into a chat or an email instead of attaching the file. Colleagues with access open this very folder, so nobody works on an old copy.</p><p>The link itself does not give anyone access.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Deck app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Deck keeps track of tasks, your own or your team's, so everyone sees who does what and what is due.</p><p>In this tour you add a task, give it a due date and see where it comes back.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Calendar app. Words in bold
#. are labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Deleted an event by mistake? It stays in the <strong>Trash bin</strong> for a while, so you can restore it.</p><p>That's it. Now plan your next real meeting here, and invite the people involved.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Deck app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Each column is a list, such as To do or Done, and each card is a task. Click the highlighted button to add one.</p><p>No button? You can only view this board, or it has no lists yet. Click <strong>Back</strong> and open another.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Talk app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Each conversation has its own setting: hover over it, click the three dots and open <strong>Notifications</strong>. Put your team's conversation on <strong>All messages</strong>.</p><p>Someone chose <strong>@-mentions only</strong>? Type <strong>@</strong> and their name to reach them.</p>"
msgstr ""

msgid "<p>Everyone gets the tour in their own language: the built-in steps are translated. To write your own text for a language, add a language override and edit its steps.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Files app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Everything shared with you or by you is under <strong>Shares</strong>. Folders shared with your group or project also show up in <strong>All files</strong>.</p><p>A share from another Nextcloud server may wait in <strong>Pending shares</strong>: open Shares with its arrow to accept it.</p>"
msgstr ""

msgid "<p>Files is where you view and manage everything you store.</p><p>You will find it in the apps menu (top left) — together with Calendar, Mail, Contacts and more. Click the menu any time to switch apps.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Files app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Files is where your work lives. Share a link instead of emailing attachments, so everyone works in the same copy.</p><p>In this tour you make a folder, see how to share it and learn how to undo mistakes.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Calendar app. Words in bold
#. are labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>For office hours, supervision or study participants: an appointment schedule gives people a link to book a free slot with you, no account needed.</p><p>See a warning here? Your account needs an email address; ask your IT team if you cannot add one.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Files app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Here you upload files, or a whole folder at once, and create new documents to work on together.</p><p>For now, choose <strong>New folder</strong>.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Talk app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>In <strong>Participants</strong> on the right (open the sidebar if needed), type a colleague's or group's name and pick them. They get a notification.</p><p>External partners? Invite them by email in a separate conversation, if your organization allows guests.</p>"
msgstr ""

msgid "<p>IntroVox gives newcomers a short tour of Nextcloud, like this one. In a minute you know how to make your own.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Deck app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Keep everything about a task on its card: notes and checklists in the description, discussion in the comments, files as attachments for everyone on the board. Type @ in a comment to mention someone.</p><p>Now close the card with ✕, then click <strong>Next</strong>.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Calendar app. Words in bold
#. are labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Let's plan something: click the highlighted button to start a new event.</p><p>Later you can also click a day in the calendar, or drag across a few hours in the week view.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Files app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Let's start with a folder of your own: click <strong>New</strong>.</p><p>No New button? Open a folder you can add to, such as a project folder.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Calendar app. Words in bold
#. are labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Make a separate calendar for a project or team, and share it with them.</p><p>If your organization allows it, you can also subscribe to a read-only calendar by link, such as a course timetable, or add public holidays.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. {manual} is a link with the text "the IntroVox manual". "Support" is the
#. name of a tab on this page: use the same translation
msgid "<p>More, such as tours across apps and steps that continue on a click, is in {manual}. This tour is under <strong>Support</strong> if you want to see it again.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Files app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Name it after something you're working on now, so it's useful right away and others see what's inside.</p><p>Click <strong>Create</strong> first, then click <strong>Next</strong>.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Talk app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Need to talk? <strong>Start call</strong> notifies everyone in the conversation, and they join with one click. You can share your screen too.</p><p>No need to try it now: it would ring them all.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Talk app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Next time you have a quick question, type a colleague's name here to start a one-to-one chat. It also finds your conversations.</p><p>That's it. Send your next team update in your team conversation instead of an email.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Talk app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Next to <strong>Start call</strong>, the calendar button lists upcoming meetings. <strong>Schedule a meeting</strong> puts one in your calendar and invites everyone here.</p><p>At meeting time, everyone opens this conversation and joins the call.</p>"
msgstr ""

msgid "<p>Nice to have you here! This short tour will help you get started quickly.</p><p>You can close this wizard at any time and open it again later.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Files app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Now click the share icon next to your new folder. Could not make one? Any folder you can share will do.</p><p>The icon opens a panel that shows who has access. Nothing gets shared yet.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Deck app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Now see your task come back: click <strong>Upcoming cards</strong>. It gathers the open cards from all your boards in one view.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Calendar app. Words in bold
#. are labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Plan meetings and time for your own work, and see when colleagues are free.</p><p>In this tour you plan an event, then see how to invite colleagues, share calendars and have them on your phone too.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Calendar app. Words in bold
#. are labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Plan something real: type what it is, such as <em>Project meeting</em> or <em>Writing time</em>.</p><p>Then set the day and time just below it, and click <strong>Next</strong>.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Calendar app. Words in bold
#. are labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Planned it for another week or month? The arrows above take you there; click the date between them to jump to any day. <strong>Today</strong> brings you back.</p><p>This menu switches between day, week, month, year and a list.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Files app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Someone at another organization? Type their email address above, or their federated cloud ID if they use Nextcloud too.</p><p>Or create a public link: its <strong>⋯</strong> menu › <strong>Customize link</strong> adds a password and an expiration date. Your organization may limit public links.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Deck app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>That's it. Ready for real work? Add a board for each project or team, give it your own lists and share it with the people involved.</p><p>The cards on the Welcome board have more tips.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Files app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>The <strong>Activity</strong> tab shows what happened to this item, such as who created, renamed or shared it.</p><p>You can also leave a comment there for everyone with access.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the tour of the IntroVox administration page. Words in
#. bold are names of tabs and buttons on that page: use the same
#. translation
msgid "<p>The <strong>welcome tour</strong> shows Nextcloud to newcomers. Add a <strong>New tour</strong> for an app, such as Talk: it starts the first time someone opens that app.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Deck app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>This button opens the board's details: share the board with colleagues, groups or teams, and see who changed what.</p><p>People you add can only view at first. Turn on <strong>Can edit</strong> for those who work on the cards.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Files app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Type a colleague's name, a group or a team. Choose <strong>View only</strong> or <strong>Allow upload and editing</strong>, then click <strong>Save share</strong>.</p><p>Anything you add to the folder later is shared too. You do not have to share anything now.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Talk app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Type the name of a team, project or research group you work with, then click <strong>Next</strong>. Leave the other options as they are.</p><p>Already have a team conversation? Close this with ✕, then click <strong>Next</strong>.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the tour of the IntroVox administration page. Words in
#. bold are names of tabs and buttons on that page: use the same
#. translation
msgid "<p>While this is on, tours start by themselves: the welcome tour for everyone who is new, and a tour for an app when someone first opens it. <strong>Show again to everyone</strong>, in the menu of a tour under <strong>Tours</strong>, shows it once more, for instance after a big change.</p>"
msgstr ""

msgid "<p>With the search bar you can quickly find files, contacts and more.</p><p>Just type what you're looking for and press Enter.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Talk app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Write a first message, for example what this conversation is for, and send it.</p><p>The <strong>+</strong> button shares one of your files, so everyone works in the same copy.</p>"
msgstr ""

msgid "<p>You're all set to get started!</p><p>If you want to see this tour again, you can find it in your personal settings.</p><p>Have fun with Nextcloud!</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Deck app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Your boards are listed here, together with boards colleagues share with you.</p><p>Click your <strong>Welcome</strong> board to practice: only you can see it. No Welcome board? Open a board of your own.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Deck app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Your new card is at the bottom of the list. Click it to open it.</p><p>Later on, drag cards to the next list as the work moves on, and up or down to change their order.</p>"
msgstr ""

#. Text of a step in the built-in tour of the Deck app. Words in bold are
#. labels in Nextcloud: use the words Nextcloud shows in your language
msgid "<p>Your open cards from every board, assigned to you or to no one, sorted by due date. Find your new card under the day you picked, or under <strong>No due</strong>.</p><p>Finished? Click <strong>Mark as done</strong> on its card, and it leaves this list.</p>"
msgstr ""

msgid "<p>Your profile, personal settings and the log out button live under your avatar (top right).</p><p>Click it whenever you want to adjust your account.</p>"
msgstr ""

